s and PRs that mix moves with logic, add dependencies, skip tests or are too big to review.",[34,72,44,78,125],"size",{"slug":127,"kind":107,"description":128,"keywords":129},"review-chain","Blocks the PR skill until code-review, ponytail-review and comment-cleanup have run in the session.",[34,78,44,49],{"slug":131,"kind":107,"description":132,"keywords":133},"stop-check","Blocks the end of a turn while a changed JS/TS project fails its typecheck or related tests.",[34,134,135,136,137],"typecheck","tests","javascript","typescript",{"slug":139,"kind":107,"description":140,"keywords":141},"text-lint","Refuses PR, issue and commit text with dashes, test plan sections, tables, hard wraps or features framed as fixes.",[34,73,44,142,111],"commit",{"slug":144,"kind":107,"description":145,"keywords":146},"worktree-guard","Refuses edits in the main checkout while another Claude session works there, and points you to a worktree.",[34,72,50,51,147],"sessions",{"slug":149,"kind":150,"description":151,"keywords":152},"context-hud","mod","Context window and plan usage limits at a glance: footer gauges, a per-category pane, and a warning past a threshold",[153,154,155,156,157],"context","tokens","usage","limits","hud",{"slug":159,"kind":150,"description":160,"keywords":161},"context-meter","Shows context size and session cost in the status line, and warns once when the context passes a threshold",[153,154,162,163],"cost","status",{"slug":165,"kind":150,"description":166,"keywords":167},"gh-guard","Blocks Claude from posting GitHub comments or reviews as you until you give an explicit go",[26,115,16,78,118],{"slug":169,"kind":150,"description":170,"keywords":171},"read-guard","Caps unbounded Reads of large files and tells Claude how to read the rest",[172,153,154,115],"read",{"slug":174,"kind":150,"description":175,"keywords":176},"secret-redactor","Swaps secrets, emails and IPs in tool output and prompts for stable placeholders, and restores real values in tool inputs",[58,119,177,178,179],"redaction","pii","privacy",{"slug":181,"kind":150,"description":182,"keywords":183},"smart-typecheck","After a turn that edited code, runs the check script once in each package that was touched",[134,137,111,56,86]],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"item":1,"related":24},{"slug":2,"kind":3,"description":4,"keywords":5,"version":10,"html":11,"skills":12,"hooks":16,"files":17,"sources":21},"pr-address-comments","skill","Pulls review comments on your PR, fixes what is actionable, and pushes, without ever writing to GitHub.",[6,7,8,9],"github","pull-request","review","comments","1.0.0","\u003Ch2>What it does\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>pr-address-comments\u003C/code> pulls the open review comments on your pull request, fixes the ones that ask for a concrete change, and pushes to the PR branch. It never replies, resolves threads, reacts, or posts anything on GitHub. Questions and disagreements come back to you in the report.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2>When to use it\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>&quot;Address the review feedback on PR 123.&quot;\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>&quot;Check the comments on my PR and fix what you can.&quot;\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2>How it works\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>Finds the PR for the current branch and checks it out.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Pulls review threads with one GraphQL call, then review summaries and conversation comments. It drops resolved, outdated and self-authored comments.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Sorts each comment as actionable, nit, question, out of scope or disagreement, and fixes only inside the comment&#39;s scope.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Runs the project&#39;s own checks, folds each fix into the commit it belongs to, and pushes with \u003Ccode>--force-with-lease\u003C/code>.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Reports what it fixed, what it skipped, and what needs your reply.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2>Requirements\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>git\u003C/code> and the GitHub CLI (\u003Ccode>gh\u003C/code>), authenticated.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n",[13],{"name":2,"description":14,"argumentHint":-1,"invocation":15},"Use when the user asks to check, review, address, or fix comments on a pull request. Pulls review threads, fixes what is actionable locally, pushes to the PR branch. NEVER replies, resolves, or posts anything to GitHub.","/pr-address-comments:pr-address-comments",[],[18,19,20],".claude-plugin/plugin.json","README.md","skills/pr-address-comments/SKILL.md",[22],{"path":20,"html":23},"\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">---\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">name\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">pr-address-comments\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">description\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">Use when the user asks to check, review, address, or fix comments on a pull request. Pulls review threads, fixes what is actionable locally, pushes to the PR branch. NEVER replies, resolves, or posts anything to GitHub.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">---\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\"># Address PR Comments\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">Pull review comments on a PR, fix what is actionable, push. Never write to GitHub.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\">## When to use\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">-\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> \"check the comments on the PR\" / \"address the review feedback\" / \"fix the comments on PR #123\"\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\">## Iron rule: never write to GitHub\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">Allowed writes: local file edits, local commits, \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`git push`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> to the PR's own branch.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">Forbidden: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`gh pr review`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`gh pr comment`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`gh api -X POST`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> on \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`/comments`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> / \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`/reviews`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, emoji reactions, thread resolution, re-requesting review, PR title / body edits unless the user asked.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">If a comment seems to need a verbal reply, surface it in the report instead. The user replies themselves.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\">## Phase 0: Identify the PR\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">```bash\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">gh\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> pr\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> view\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> --json\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> number,headRefName,baseRefName,url,state\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">```\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">If the current branch has no PR, ask. If the PR is closed/merged, stop. Otherwise:\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">```bash\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">gh\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> pr\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> checkout\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> &#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">numbe\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">r\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">>\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">```\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\">## Phase 1: Pull comments\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">One GraphQL call covers most of what you need:\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">```bash\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">gh\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> api\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> graphql\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -f\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> query='\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62